-- title:
--   Mazur admissibility of the Eisenstein-primary q^m-torsion of J₀(p)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, and assume `HeckeOperatorsCommuteBar p`: the endomorphisms `heckeOperatorBar p ℓ` of `JZero p` (the group of degree-zero divisor classes, $\mathrm{Pic}^0$, of the level-$p$ modular function field base changed to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) commute pairwise as $\ell$ ranges over the primes. Let $q$ be a prime and $m$ a natural number. Let $A =$ `eisensteinPrimaryTorsionBar p q m` be the subgroup of `JZero p` consisting of the elements killed by $q^m$ which, for the action of $\mathbb T = \mathbb Z[T_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ given by `heckeModuleBar p`, also lie in the union over $k$ of the submodules killed by the $k$-th power of the Eisenstein maximal ideal `eisensteinMaximalIdeal p q` (the preimage under `eisensteinEval` of the ideal generated by $q$). The assertion is that there exists an `OpenAction` $\Phi$ on $A$, that is a monoid homomorphism $\Phi.\varphi$ from $\overline{\mathbb Q} \simeq_{\mathbb Q} \overline{\mathbb Q}$ to the additive automorphisms of $A$ whose kernel is open, such that $\Phi.\varphi(\sigma)(x) = \sigma \cdot x$ in `JZero p` for all $\sigma$ and all $x \in A$, and such that `AdmissibleChain q Φ` is nonempty: there are $n$, subgroups $A_0 \le \cdots$ indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}(n+1)$ with $A_0 = 0$, $A_n = A$ and $A_i \le A_{i+1}$, and tags $t_i \in \{\text{true},\text{false}\}$, such that each quotient $A_{i+1}/A_i$ has cardinality exactly $q$, and for each $i$: if $t_i$ is true then $\Phi.\varphi(\sigma)(x) - x \in A_i$ for every $\sigma$ and every $x \in A_{i+1}$, while if $t_i$ is false then $\Phi.\varphi(\sigma)(x) - a x \in A_i$ for every $\sigma$, every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, every $a$ with $\sigma\zeta = \zeta^a$, and every $x \in A_{i+1}$.
--
--   This is the admissibility, in Mazur's sense, of the Eisenstein-primary part of the $q^m$-torsion of $J_0(p)$: the Galois module is filtered by subgroups with quotients of order $q$ on which Galois acts trivially or through the mod-$q$ cyclotomic character. It is the carrier variant, for the $\mathfrak P$-primary $q^m$-torsion rather than the $\mathfrak P^m$-torsion, of [`ModularCurve.eisensteinPrimaryTorsion_isMazurAdmissible_heckeModuleBar`](thm.html#ModularCurve.eisensteinPrimaryTorsion_isMazurAdmissible_heckeModuleBar), and supplies the Galois input to the construction of Jordan–Hölder flags and Kummer rows used downstream.
